    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1153">

                <pb facs="1347" n="1151" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1151"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Truman Papers</note>
                <head>No. 1153<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dunn</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1153-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Potsdam</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-31">July 31, 1945</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Would it<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1153-f2"/> be appropriate for the Polish
                    Government officials to be jointly notified of the decision on the Polish
                    boundary. You might have one representative of each of the three to do it
                    here.</p>
                <closer><signed>J[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ames</hi>] C[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">lement</hi>] D[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >unn</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1153-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1153-f1-content">
                <p>This paper is a manuscript note in pencil which Dunn apparently passed to Byrnes
                    in the course of the Eleventh Plenary Meeting, July 31 (see <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg528">p. 528</ref>), and which
                    Byrnes, with the change described in footnote 2, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >infra</hi>, apparently passed on to Truman with the manuscript notation,
                    “from Dunn”.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1153-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1153-f2-content">
                <p>Byrnes amended the first sentence by hand to read: “Would it not”.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
